== Research Summary

- Signal detection and estimation
- Radio map construction and application
- Integrated sensing and communications
- Wireless sensor network
- Resource allocation
- Deep learning based radar signal processing


=== Signal detection and estimation
- [https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/11676079/ Noncoherent detection of constant-envelope signals for mobile edge applications—asymptotically optimal detectors and a reliability-based intelligent detector] (IEEE Transactions on Mobile Computing, 2026).

=== Radio map Construction and Application
- [https://doi.org/10.1109/ICCWorkshops63917.2026.11586741 Physics-aware tensor reconstruction for radio maps in pixel-based fluid antenna systems] (IEEE ICC Workshops, 2026).
- [https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.15560 Privacy-preserving federated radio map learning for wireless digital twins via adaptive noise allocation] (IEEE SPAWC, 2026; [https://2026.ieeespawc.org/technical-program/ Paper ID 241]).
- Discovering CSI evolution using radio map for massive MIMO channel estimation (ICC 2024).
- Antenna pattern calibration in low-altitude air-to-ground sensing via radio map (ICCC Workshops 2024).

=== ISAC & WSN
- [https://doi.org/10.1109/TNSE.2025.3649043 UAV detection and localization: A RF-based framework via multiple stations collaboration] (IEEE TNSE, 2026; *co-first author*).
- Resource optimization in wireless sensing and localization networks (Applied Sciences 2024).
- Scheduling in wireless cooperative localization networks with intelligent eavesdroppers (WCMC 2024).
- Power allocation in infrastructure-limited integrated sensing and localization networks (VTC 2022-Fall).
- Multipath ghosts mitigation for radar-based positioning systems (VTC 2022-Fall).
- Reliable target positioning in complicated environments using multiple radar observations (GLOBECOM 2021).

=== Radar signal processing & machine learning
- Multipath ghosts mitigation for radar-based positioning systems (VTC 2022-Fall).
- Reliable target positioning in complicated environments using multiple radar observations (GLOBECOM 2021).
- Human activity classification with radar signal processing and machine learning (UCET 2020).
- Elderly care: deep learning for multi-domain activity classification (UCET 2020).

